 "lines": [
  "The warm car was the trap.",
  "A blizzard. Kai and Leo are stuck on the highway, snow piling up.",
  "@am_echo: \"It's freezing. Keep the heater on all night!\"",
  "But snow is drifting over the back of the car. Over the tailpipe.",
  "With nowhere to go, the exhaust builds up inside the car.",
  "It carries carbon monoxide. No color. No smell.",
  "In one fire department test, the alarm went off in under ninety seconds.",
  "@am_echo: \"Why do I have a headache?\"",
  "Headache. Dizziness. Confusion. Then sleepiness.",
  "Carbon monoxide grabs your blood over two hundred times more easily than oxygen.",
  "So your body starves for oxygen, even as you breathe.",
  "@am_echo: \"I'm just gonna [close](cloze) my eyes.\"",
  "People who fall asleep can die before they ever feel the symptoms.",
  "@am_michael: \"Leo! Wake up! Engine off!\"",
  "Kai shuts off the engine, opens a window, and digs out the tailpipe.",
  "If you're stranded, stay with your car. Run the engine only about ten minutes an hour.",
  "Clear the exhaust pipe first. A cracked window helps, but it's not enough alone.",
  "@am_echo: \"So the heater almost got us?\"",
  "It's real. In the Blizzard of seventy-eight, about thirty-five hundred cars and trucks got stuck near Boston.",
  "Some kept their engines running as snow buried their tailpipes, and died of carbon monoxide.",
  "@am_michael: \"Clear the tailpipe, Leo. Every time. Because sometimes...\""
 ],
